,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_plug_template=>4073835273271169698
,p_plug_display_sequence=>20
,p_plug_item_display_point=>'ABOVE'
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<div class="wss-Doc">',
'<h3>Build a website in 10 minutes</h3>',
'<ol>',
'  <li><strong>Pick a starting point.</strong> In the Gallery, open the starter website closest to yours (company, restaurant, clinic, real estate, event, portfolio, SaaS) and press <em>Customize</em>.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Choose the look.</strong> In the Designer, change Design, Accent Color, Typeface and Header until it feels right. Press <em>Copy APEXlang</em>, or note the options listed under <em>Your Choice</em>.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Copy the page.</strong> In Website Studio, <strong>Page Designer &gt; Create &gt; Page as Copy</strong> of that starter page (into your own application after step 2 of the next section), give it a name, and set the Template Options you '
||'chose.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Change the words.</strong> Every section is a region: change titles in Page Designer, and the rows in each region''s SQL query (or point the query at your own table).</li>',
'  <li><strong>Add your photos.</strong> Upload them to <strong>Shared Components &gt; Static Application Files</strong> and put the file names in <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> (see <em>Pictures</em> below).</li>',
'  <li><strong>Set the menu.</strong> Edit the list under <strong>Shared Components &gt; Lists</strong> (for example <em>Company - Menu</em>): its entries are the header menu.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Make the form yours.</strong> Change the process <em>Send Message</em> to email or store the message (the code is in its comments).</li>',
'</ol>',
'',
'<h3>1. Get Website Studio into your workspace</h3>',
'<ol>',
'  <li>Download <code>website-studio.sql</code> from <a href="https://github.com/HashaamShoukat/apex-website-studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> (or import the APEXlang source with SQLcl: <code>apex import -input apexlang</code>).</li>',
'  <li><strong>App Builder &gt; Import</strong>, install it with any application ID. No database objects; APEX 26.1 or later.</li>',
'</ol>',
'',
'<h3>2. Copy the templates into your application</h3>',
'<p>In <em>your</em> application: <strong>Shared Components &gt; Templates &gt; Create &gt; As a Copy of an Existing Template</strong>, copy from <strong>Website Studio</strong> (tick <em>Subscribe</em> for later updates):</p>',
'<table>',
'  <tr><th>Type</th><th>Template</th><th>Use it for</th></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Page</td><td>Modern One Page</td><td>The website page: header, menu, hero, sections, footer.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Region</td><td>Modern Section</td><td>Every band of the page. The region title is the heading, the Static ID the menu anchor.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>List</td><td>Website - Menu</td><td>The header menu, with drop-downs for child entries.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Report</td><td>Website - Hero, Numbers, Services, Team, Testimonials, Logos, Pricing, Timeline, Process, FAQ, Careers, Portfolio, Links, Contact Details, News, Products, Photo Gallery, Image and Text, Events, Opening Hours, Comparison, Vide'
||'o, Map</td><td>Classic Report templates: each turns the rows of a SQL query into a section.</td></tr>',
'</table>',
'<p>The templates load their CSS and JavaScript from static files, which the copy does not bring along. Upload <code>website-studio/website.css</code> and <code>website-studio/website.js</code> to <strong>Shared Components &gt; Static Application File'
||'s</strong> in your application, in a directory named <code>website-studio</code>. Download them from Website Studio''s own Static Application Files, or from <code>apexlang/shared-components/static-files/website-studio</code> on GitHub.</p>',
'',
'<h3>3. Build the page</h3>',
'<ol>',
'  <li>Create a blank page and set <strong>Appearance &gt; Page Template</strong> to <strong>Modern One Page</strong>. Make it public if visitors should not sign in. Pick the Template Options you built in the Designer.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Hero</strong>: a Classic Report in the <em>Hero</em> slot. Region template <strong>Modern Section</strong> with Spacing <em>None</em>, Width <em>Full Width</em>, Heading <em>Hidden</em>; report template <strong>Website - Hero</strong>. '
||'One row per slide.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Sections</strong>: regions in the <em>Body</em> slot with the <strong>Modern Section</strong> template. Give each a <strong>Static ID</strong> (it becomes <code>#services</code> in the menu).</li>',
'  <li><strong>Lists of things</strong>: make the region a <strong>Classic Report</strong>, write the SQL with the column names below, and set <strong>Attributes &gt; Appearance &gt; Template</strong> to the matching Website report template. Set <em>N'
||'umber of Rows</em> high enough (the starters use 100) and pagination to <em>No Pagination</em>. APEX does not keep the order of the query, so add a column such as <code>SORT_ORDER</code> and set its <em>Sorting &gt; Default Sequence</em> to 1 (the te'
||'mplates do not show it).</li>',
'  <li><strong>Free text</strong> (about, vision, call to action): a Static Content region with the helper classes below.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Contact form</strong>: page items and a button in a Modern Section region with the CSS class <code>ws-Contact</code>, and a process that stores or emails the message. Put a <em>Website - Contact Details</em> report in its Sub Regions.</'
||'li>',
'  <li><strong>Footer</strong>: regions with the <em>Blank with Attributes</em> template in the <em>Footer</em> slot (a <em>Website - Links</em> report with layout List makes a link column) and <em>Footer Bottom</em> for the copyright line.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Logo</strong>: a Static Content region in the <em>Logo</em> slot (or the application logo).</li>',
'</ol>',
'',
'<h3>4. The menu</h3>',
'<p>Create a <strong>List</strong> (<strong>Shared Components &gt; Lists</strong>), then a <strong>List</strong> region in the page''s <strong>Menu</strong> slot with region template <em>Blank with Attributes</em> and list template <strong>Website - Me'
||'nu</strong>.</p>',
'<ul>',
'  <li>Entries with a URL like <code>#services</code> scroll to that section and light up while it is on screen. Entries can also go to other pages or other websites.</li>',
'  <li>Child entries (<em>Parent List Entry</em>) open as a drop-down on wide screens (hover, click or the keyboard; Escape closes) and as an accordion on phones.</li>',
'  <li><em>User Defined Attribute 1</em>: extra CSS classes (<code>ws-Menu-cta</code> makes a button). <em>Attribute 2</em>: link target (<code>_blank</code> for a new tab). For a new tab add <code>rel="noopener"</code> in <em>Link Attributes</em>.</l'
||'i>',
'  <li>Template Options: <em>Alignment</em>, <em>Visible Entries</em> (the rest go into More), <em>On Phones</em> (drop-down, full-screen overlay or side drawer) and <em>Last Entry as Button</em>.</li>',
'  <li>No list region? The menu is built from the Modern Section regions with <em>Show in Menu</em>.</li>',
'</ul>',
'<p>A list can also come from a table (<strong>List Source = SQL Query</strong>). The restaurant starter does this:</p>',
'<pre>select level, label, target,',
'       null as is_current, null as image, null as image_attribute, null as image_alt,',
'       null as attribute1, link_target as attribute2',
'  from my_menu',
' start with parent_id is null',
'connect by prior id = parent_id',
' order siblings by seq</pre>',
'<p><strong>A website with several pages.</strong> Give every page the Modern One Page template with the same Template Options, and put the same list in each page''s Menu slot (<em>Copy to other Page</em> copies the menu, logo and footer regions). Then'
||':</p>',
'<ul>',
'  <li>Let the list entries go to pages (<em>Target Type: Page in this Application</em>). APEX marks the entry of the page that is open.</li>',
'  <li>A child entry can open a section of another page: URL <code>f?p=&amp;APP_ID.:SERVICES:&amp;APP_SESSION.#faq</code>.</li>',
'  <li>Links in reports (footer columns, buttons, "read more") come from the query: <code>apex_page.get_url(p_page =&gt; ''SERVICES'') as link</code>. In Static Content, use <code>f?p=&amp;APP_ID.:SERVICES:&amp;APP_SESSION.</code>; point the logo to the'
||' home page.</li>',
'  <li>Inner pages open with a short title band: a Website - Hero region with one row, Layout <em>Full Bleed</em> and Height <em>Compact (page title)</em>.</li>',
'  <li>Put the contact form on one page only and link to it from the others.</li>',
'</ul>',
'<p>The 4 multi-page starters in the Gallery (pages 20 to 53) show all of this.</p>',
'',
'<h3>5. Pictures</h3>',
'<p>Every template that shows a picture has the same columns: <code>IMAGE_URL</code>, <code>IMAGE_FILE</code>, <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> (what the picture shows, read aloud by screen readers) and <code>IMAGE_POSITION</code> (the part to keep when it is c'
||'ropped, like <code>center 30%</code> or <code>top</code>). Pictures load when they scroll into view. A row without a picture shows a soft placeholder (Template Option <em>Placeholder Images</em>), and people show their initials. There are three ways '
||'to give a picture:</p>',
'<p><strong>a. A URL</strong> - any https address:</p>',
'<pre>select ''https://images.example.com/team/sara.jpg'' as image_url,',
'       ''Sara in the studio'' as image_alt, name, role',
'  from team_members</pre>',
'<p><strong>b. A Static Application File</strong> - upload it to <strong>Shared Components &gt; Static Application Files</strong>, then give its name in <code>IMAGE_FILE</code>. The starter websites use <code>website-studio/img/...</code>:</p>',
'<pre>select ''We design brands people *remember*.'' as title,',
'       ''Brand and digital studio'' as subtitle,',
'       ''Strategy, identity and websites.'' as text,',
'       ''website-studio/img/studio-hero-1.jpg'' as image_file,',
'       ''Designers around a table'' as image_alt,',
'       ''center 40%'' as image_position,',
'       ''See our work'' as button_label,',
'       ''#work'' as button_link,',
'       1 as sort_order',
'  from dual</pre>',
'<p><strong>c. A BLOB column</strong> - keep the photo in your own table. Create an <strong>Application Item</strong> <code>IMG_ID</code> (Session State Protection: <em>Unrestricted</em>) and an <strong>Application Process</strong> <code>GET_IMAGE</co'
||'de> (Point: <em>Ajax Callback</em>, no authentication needed for public pages):</p>',
'<pre>declare',
'    l_photo blob;',
'    l_mime  varchar2(255);',
'begin',
'    select photo, mime_type into l_photo, l_mime',
'      from team_members',
'     where id = :IMG_ID;',
'    sys.owa_util.mime_header(l_mime, false);',
'    sys.htp.p(''Cache-Control: max-age=86400'');',
'    sys.owa_util.http_header_close;',
'    sys.wpg_docload.download_file(l_photo);',
'    apex_application.stop_apex_engine;',
'end;</pre>',
'<p>Then return its URL in <code>IMAGE_URL</code>:</p>',
'<pre>select name, role,',
'       ''f?p='' || :APP_ID || '':0:'' || :APP_SESSION || '':APPLICATION_PROCESS=GET_IMAGE:::IMG_ID:'' || id as image_url',
'  from team_members</pre>',
'<p>The hero also takes <code>VIDEO_URL</code>: an <code>.mp4</code> or <code>.webm</code> file plays silently behind the slide. The <em>Video</em> template takes YouTube and Vimeo links and loads the player only when the visitor presses play.</p>',
'',
'<h3>6. The report templates and their columns</h3>',
'<p>Every column is optional: a column the query does not return is simply left out. <code>ICON</code> takes a Font APEX class such as <code>fa-lightbulb-o</code>; brand icons (<code>fa-instagram</code>, <code>fa-linkedin</code>, <code>fa-x-twitter</c'
||'ode>, <code>fa-youtube-play</code>, <code>fa-facebook</code>, <code>fa-github</code>, <code>fa-tiktok</code>, <code>fa-whatsapp</code> ...) are drawn by Website Studio, because Font APEX has none.</p>',
'<table>',
'  <tr><th>Template</th><th>What it is</th><th>Columns</th></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Hero</td><td>The opening section. One row is one slide; with more than one row it becomes a slider. VIDEO_URL (an .mp4 or .webm file) plays muted behind the text, with the image as its poster.</td><td><code>TITLE</code> <code>SUBT'
||'ITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IMAGE_POSITION</code> <code>VIDEO_URL</code> <code>BUTTON_LABEL</code> <code>BUTTON_LINK</code> <code>BUTTON2_LABEL</code> <code>BUTTON2_LINK</c'
||'ode></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Numbers</td><td>Key figures that count up when they scroll into view (page option Count Up Numbers).</td><td><code>VALUE</code> <code>PREFIX</code> <code>SUFFIX</code> <code>LABEL</code> <code>TEXT</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Services</td><td>Services, features or benefits. ICON is a Font APEX class such as fa-lightbulb-o.</td><td><code>ICON</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>LINK</code> <code>LINK_LABEL</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Team</td><td>People with a photo (or their initials), role and a profile link. LINK_ICON defaults to fa-linkedin.</td><td><code>NAME</code> <code>ROLE</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <c'
||'ode>IMAGE_POSITION</code> <code>BIO</code> <code>LINK</code> <code>LINK_ICON</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Testimonials</td><td>What customers say. RATING is 0 to 5 stars (empty hides the stars).</td><td><code>QUOTE</code> <code>NAME</code> <code>ROLE</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IM'
||'AGE_POSITION</code> <code>RATING</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Logos</td><td>Clients, partners or press. Without an image the name is shown as a word mark.</td><td><code>NAME</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>LINK</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Pricing</td><td>Plans. FEATURES is one feature per line (or separated by | or ;). IS_FEATURED = Y highlights a plan.</td><td><code>NAME</code> <code>PRICE</code> <code>PERIOD</code> <code>DESCRIPTION</code> <code>FEATURES</code> <'
||'code>BUTTON_LABEL</code> <code>BUTTON_LINK</code> <code>IS_FEATURED</code> <code>BADGE</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Timeline</td><td>Milestones of your history.</td><td><code>YEAR</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Process</td><td>How you work, numbered in the order of the rows.</td><td><code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>DURATION</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - FAQ</td><td>Questions that open to show the answer.</td><td><code>QUESTION</code> <code>ANSWER</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Careers</td><td>Open roles that open to show the description and an apply button. Filter Buttons groups them by TEAM.</td><td><code>TITLE</code> <code>TEAM</code> <code>LOCATION</code> <code>TYPE</code> <code>DESCRIPTION</code> <c'
||'ode>APPLY_LINK</code> <code>APPLY_LABEL</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Portfolio</td><td>Projects with a picture and a link. Filter Buttons groups them by CATEGORY.</td><td><code>TITLE</code> <code>CATEGORY</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IMAGE_POSIT'
||'ION</code> <code>LINK</code> <code>META</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Links</td><td>Social media icons, footer link lists or link tiles. ICON is a Font APEX class such as fa-instagram.</td><td><code>LABEL</code> <code>LINK</code> <code>ICON</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Contact Details</td><td>Address, phone, email and opening hours. LINK makes the value a link (mailto:, tel:, a map URL).</td><td><code>ICON</code> <code>LABEL</code> <code>VALUE</code> <code>LINK</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - News</td><td>News or blog posts. POST_DATE is shown as it comes from the query (format it with to_char).</td><td><code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IMAG'
||'E_POSITION</code> <code>POST_DATE</code> <code>CATEGORY</code> <code>LINK</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Products</td><td>Products, or the dishes of a menu, with a price. Filter Buttons groups them by CATEGORY.</td><td><code>NAME</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>PRICE</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_AL'
||'T</code> <code>IMAGE_POSITION</code> <code>CATEGORY</code> <code>BADGE</code> <code>LINK</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Photo Gallery</td><td>Photos that open full size in a lightbox (arrow keys, swipe, Escape closes).</td><td><code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IMAGE_POSITION</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>'
||'CAPTION</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Image and Text</td><td>Rows of a picture next to text, alternating sides (zig-zag).</td><td><code>EYEBROW</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IMAG'
||'E_POSITION</code> <code>LINK</code> <code>LINK_LABEL</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Events</td><td>An agenda or events list. EVENT_DATE and EVENT_TIME are shown as they come from the query.</td><td><code>EVENT_DATE</code> <code>EVENT_TIME</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>LOCATION</code> <code>SPE'
||'AKER</code> <code>LINK</code> <code>LINK_LABEL</code> <code>CATEGORY</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Opening Hours</td><td>Opening hours. DAY_NUMBER (1 = Monday ... 7 = Sunday) highlights today; without it the day name is compared with today''s name.</td><td><code>DAY_NAME</code> <code>HOURS</code> <code>NOTE</code> <code>DAY_NUMB'
||'ER</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Comparison</td><td>A comparison table: one row per feature, one column per plan (COL1 to COL4). The row with IS_HEADER = Y holds the plan names. Y and N become a tick and a dash.</td><td><code>FEATURE</code> <code>COL1</code> <cod'
||'e>COL2</code> <code>COL3</code> <code>COL4</code> <code>IS_HEADER</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Video</td><td>Videos from YouTube, Vimeo or an .mp4 file. Nothing loads until the visitor presses play; the image is the cover.</td><td><code>VIDEO_URL</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>IMAGE_URL</code> <code>IMAGE'
||'_FILE</code> <code>IMAGE_ALT</code> <code>IMAGE_POSITION</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Website - Map</td><td>A map from an embed URL (Google Maps or OpenStreetMap) next to the address. The map loads when it scrolls into view.</td><td><code>MAP_URL</code> <code>TITLE</code> <code>ADDRESS</code> <code>TEXT</code> <code>LINK</co'
||'de> <code>LINK_LABEL</code></td></tr>',
'</table>',
'',
'<h3>7. Helper classes for Static Content</h3>',
'<table>',
'  <tr><th>Class</th><th>What it does</th></tr>',
'  <tr><td><code>ws-Eyebrow</code>, <code>ws-Lead</code></td><td>At the start of a Modern Section''s <em>Header</em> text: a small label above the heading and an intro below it.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td><code>*word*</code> in a title</td><td>Highlights the word in the accent colour (italic with the serif typefaces).</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td><code>ws-Split</code>, <code>ws-Split--reverse</code></td><td>Two columns, for example <code>&lt;div class="ws-Media" data-file="website-studio/img/studio.jpg" role="img" aria-label="Our studio"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code> next to a <code>ws-Sta'
||'ck</code> of text.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td><code>ws-Title</code>, <code>ws-Display</code>, <code>ws-Statement</code></td><td>Section heading, hero-size heading, a large statement.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td><code>ws-Btn</code>, <code>ws-Btn--ghost</code>, <code>ws-More</code>, <code>ws-Actions</code></td><td>Buttons, a text link with an arrow, a row of buttons.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td><code>ws-Checks</code>, <code>ws-Pillars</code>, <code>ws-Center</code></td><td>A list with check marks, a row of short columns, centred content.</td></tr>',
'</table>',
'',
'<h3>8. Arabic and right to left</h3>',
'<p>The templates use logical CSS, so a page in a right-to-left language mirrors itself: menu, sliders, arrows, drawers and the WhatsApp button. Run the application in Arabic (<strong>Globalization &gt; Application Primary Language</strong>, or a tran'
||'slated application) and APEX sets <code>dir="rtl"</code>; the Arabic clinic starter sets it from its <em>HTML Header</em> instead, so it works in an English application too. Pick the Typeface <em>Arabic</em> (IBM Plex Sans Arabic). Texts such as "Men'
||'u" and "Back to top" are built in for Arabic; for other languages create the text messages <code>WEBSITE_STUDIO.MENU</code>, <code>.BACK_TO_TOP</code>, <code>.ALL</code>, <code>.PREVIOUS</code>, <code>.NEXT</code>, <code>.SLIDE</code>, <code>.APPLY</'
||'code>, <code>.MORE</code>, <code>.CLOSE</code>, <code>.PLAY</code>, <code>.DARK_MODE</code> and <code>.MAP</code>.</p>',
'',
'<h3>9. WhatsApp, light and dark, search engines, spam</h3>',
'<ul>',
'  <li><strong>WhatsApp Button</strong> (page Template Option): a floating button that opens a chat. The number is the substitution string <code>WHATSAPP_NUMBER</code> in <strong>Shared Components &gt; Application Definition</strong>, in international'
||' format, digits only (<code>966500000000</code>). Without digits the button hides itself.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Light/Dark Toggle</strong>: a button in the header; the visitor''s choice is remembered in the browser.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Search engines</strong>: put a short description and Open Graph tags in the page''s <strong>HTML Header</strong> - every starter does: <code>&lt;meta name="description" content="..."&gt;</code>, <code>og:title</code>, <code>og:descriptio'
||'n</code>, <code>og:image</code>. For <code>og:image</code> use a full https address when you can: link previews in WhatsApp and LinkedIn need it. Give the page a clear <strong>Title</strong>, use <code>IMAGE_ALT</code>, and turn on <strong>Friendly U'
||'RLs</strong> in the application''s definition.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Speed</strong>: pictures load as they scroll into view; the starters preload the first hero picture with <code>&lt;link rel="preload" as="image" href="&#35;APP_FILES&#35;website-studio/img/..."&gt;</code> in the HTML Header. Keep photos'
||' under about 300 KB (1600 px wide for heroes, 800 px for cards).</li>',
'  <li><strong>Spam</strong>: the starters add a hidden field (<code>P11_WEBSITE</code>, CSS class <code>ws-Honeypot</code> on its column). People never see it; robots fill it in, and the process then sends nothing.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Sending the message</strong>: the process <em>Send Message</em> has an <code>apex_mail.send</code> example in its comments. Email needs the instance''s mail settings (ask your APEX administrator).</li>',
'</ul>',
'',
'<h3>10. Good to know</h3>',
'<ul>',
'  <li>The demo website (page <code>WEBSITE</code>) the starter websites (pages 11 to 17) and the multi-page websites (pages 20 to 53) are the best reference. Every query is a plain <code>select ... from dual</code> you can replace with your own table'
||'s.</li>',
'  <li>Typefaces other than System load from Google Fonts.</li>',
'  <li>After a partial page refresh of a section, call <code>wsSite.refresh(element)</code> - the templates already do it for <code>apexafterrefresh</code>.</li>',
'  <li>Visitors who prefer reduced motion get no animations; Windows high-contrast mode is respected; the menu, sliders, lightbox and accordions work with the keyboard. The source is in <code>apexlang/_src</code> on GitHub - edit there and run <code>n'
||'ode _src/build.mjs</code>.</li>',
'</ul>',
